# Build context trim for `docker build -f docker/Dockerfile .` (root context, whole tree).
#
# docker/Dockerfile deliberately does `COPY . .` rather than listing modules: the reactor's modules
# are unpublished 1.0.0-SNAPSHOTs that can only be built from the sources beside them, and a module
# list would have to be edited every time one is added. This file is what makes that cheap — it drops
# everything the build does not need, so adding a module stays free and no stale output leaks in.

.git
.gitignore

# Maven / Quarkus build output — regenerated inside the build stage, and ~119 MB of it here. Copying
# it in would also risk a stale target/ shadowing what the stage compiles.
**/target
**/target-ide

# Local env / IDE cruft
.env
.idea
.vscode
.settings
.factorypath
*.iml
.sdkmanrc

# Docs and the docker/ dir itself: nothing in the build reads them, and keeping them out means
# editing this Dockerfile or a README does not bust the `COPY . .` layer. docs/openapi.yml is a
# generated artefact of the test suite, which this stage does not run.
*.md
docs
docker
